01:36.110 --> 01:38.740
Soda and Napoléon clash in midair!

01:38.740 --> 01:40.740
Soda receives a warning.

01:41.220 --> 01:43.830
It's Soda's second yellow card of the game.

01:43.830 --> 01:45.740
He's being sent off!

01:45.740 --> 01:50.170
Even though you were all selected nationally to play in this tournament as the best from Japan,

01:50.170 --> 01:56.600
I honestly didn't know if you were good enough to challenge the world's best,

01:56.600 --> 02:01.110
but you've progressed magnificently in a very short time.

02:01.110 --> 02:04.740
You already know what to do.

02:04.740 --> 02:08.740
Everything will be decided during this extra time. Give it your all!

02:08.740 --> 02:10.090
Yes!

02:11.680 --> 02:16.400
For Soda's sake, we absolutely have to win and go to the final tomorrow!

02:16.400 --> 02:18.820
Yeah!

02:20.660 --> 02:25.820
<b>The Glorious Shootout</b>

02:20.660 --> 02:25.820
<b>The Glorious Shootout</b>

02:38.060 --> 02:39.580
Pierre attacks by dribbling.

02:39.580 --> 02:41.500
Let's duel, Pierre!

02:41.500 --> 02:44.500
Come on, Misaki! Let's finish what we started!

02:44.500 --> 02:46.500
All right, let's do it!

02:50.070 --> 02:51.690
Napoléon takes the loose ball!

02:51.690 --> 02:55.220
The Goddess of Victory seems to be smiling upon us.

02:55.600 --> 02:57.100
Take this!

02:57.100 --> 02:58.900
I'll stop it!

03:02.660 --> 03:07.020
The extra time ends without either team scoring,

03:07.020 --> 03:11.690
but the Japanese goal keeper, Wakashimazu, seems to have hurt his right hand.

03:11.690 --> 03:14.770
By the looks of it, France has an advantage for the second half.

03:14.770 --> 03:15.890
Tsubasa,

03:16.520 --> 03:21.750
I've come to France to witness your first international exploits.

03:21.750 --> 03:26.630
Fight hard, Tsubasa! And make sure you qualify for the final!

03:27.300 --> 03:29.520
Are you okay, Wakashimazu?

03:29.520 --> 03:32.700
Yeah, I am. There's no way we'll lose after coming this far!

03:33.340 --> 03:36.540
All right. Let's win this game at all costs!

03:36.540 --> 03:38.280
Yeah!

03:40.020 --> 03:42.300
France shoots for the fourth time!

03:42.300 --> 03:45.300
Wakashimazu stops Pierre's shot with elegance!

03:45.300 --> 03:49.340
Oh, but France recovers the ball, and it goes to Pierre!

03:46.300 --> 03:48.840
Good luck, Tsubasa-kun!

03:49.340 --> 03:50.100
Ishizaki arrives!

03:50.740 --> 03:52.540
Pierre dodges and passes!

04:03.840 --> 04:04.960
Wakabayashi!

04:05.890 --> 04:09.650
Please let Wakashimazu stay in goal until the end of this game.

04:11.740 --> 04:12.900
I've got it!

04:12.900 --> 04:17.470
Bossi takes the chance and shoots with Wakashimazu still on the ground!

04:17.470 --> 04:18.300
No way!

04:18.800 --> 04:19.380
Damn it!

04:21.910 --> 04:23.570
Get up, Wakashimazu!

04:23.570 --> 04:25.660
There's nobody other than you who can defend our goal!

04:27.780 --> 04:30.060
Hang in there, Japan! Please stop them!

04:31.780 --> 04:33.620
Wakashimazu clears!

04:34.670 --> 04:36.180
Go for it, Tsubasa-kun!

04:36.750 --> 04:37.830
All right!

04:37.830 --> 04:39.560
Ohzora has the ball.

04:39.560 --> 04:42.570
He has to attack now, but there's little time left.

04:42.570 --> 04:44.580
Run, Misaki! Run, Ohzora!

04:56.380 --> 04:57.700
Tsubasa!

05:01.860 --> 05:03.270
Roberto!

05:05.540 --> 05:06.780
Here I go!

05:06.780 --> 05:08.180
Ohzora crosses!

05:08.180 --> 05:09.380
Yes! A direct shot!

05:09.380 --> 05:10.300
The ball goes toward Misaki!

05:10.300 --> 05:11.540
I won't let you!

05:15.260 --> 05:16.180
Damn!

05:16.180 --> 05:18.760
Misaki makes a backwards pass towards the running Hyuga!

05:18.760 --> 05:20.220
I'll score!

05:32.220 --> 05:34.220
And time's up.

05:34.220 --> 05:36.400
The extra time ends with a draw.

05:36.400 --> 05:38.990
The game will be decided with a shootout.

05:46.080 --> 05:48.600
Pierre played seriously.

05:49.240 --> 05:52.020
That means his opponents are formidable.

05:52.540 --> 05:53.610
Roberto!

05:55.690 --> 05:57.430
You really came, Roberto.

05:57.430 --> 06:00.120
Hey, it's been a while, Barbas.

06:00.120 --> 06:03.280
Just as you predicted, we weren't strong enough for Japan.

06:03.280 --> 06:06.860
Argentina got knocked out of the tournament.

06:07.340 --> 06:13.380
It'd be too much of a shame to let good talent like Ohzora Tsubasa's stay in Japan.

06:16.960 --> 06:18.340
Thank you.

06:17.380 --> 06:18.340
Wakashimazu.

06:18.860 --> 06:20.820
How do you feel? Do you want to be replaced?

06:22.350 --> 06:23.960
I've come this far,

06:23.960 --> 06:27.460
so I'll do whatever it takes to defend our goal, no matter what happens.

06:36.560 --> 06:39.900
Five players from each team will take part in this penalty shootout.

06:38.850 --> 06:39.900
France gets the ball!

06:39.900 --> 06:42.930
Fate has decided that France will be the first team to shoot.

06:47.300 --> 06:50.420
We've done our best to come this far. We have to win!

06:50.420 --> 06:51.220
Yeah!

06:51.770 --> 06:53.000
Wakashimazu!

06:53.000 --> 06:53.650
Yes.

06:54.650 --> 06:56.380
We're counting on you, Wakashimazu!

06:56.380 --> 06:57.580
Wakashimazu!

07:05.780 --> 07:09.860
I'll do whatever it takes to stop these penalties!

07:10.350 --> 07:13.500
Wakashimazu, it must be hard, but keep it up.

07:13.500 --> 07:15.740
This is where the keeper has to stand firm.

07:16.180 --> 07:18.540
Pierre-sama!

07:18.540 --> 07:22.340
The first one to shoot will be France's captain, Pierre.

07:22.340 --> 07:27.060
The first penalty kick may be a decisive factor in who reaches the final.

07:27.060 --> 07:32.290
As expected, Pierre, the field artist, will shoot this important shot.

07:32.780 --> 07:36.460
Opposing him is Wakashimazu, defending the Japanese goal.

07:36.460 --> 07:40.750
Even though his right hand is injured, he needs to defend the goal somehow!

07:47.190 --> 07:51.060
As the captain of France's team, I'll score on the first penalty!

07:54.300 --> 07:54.980
Over there!

07:56.780 --> 07:57.850
It's in!

07:57.850 --> 07:59.910
Wakashimazu went the wrong way!

07:59.910 --> 08:03.180
Damn! He shot in the opposite direction of his pivot foot!

08:03.180 --> 08:06.310
Bravo, Pierre-sama!

08:09.870 --> 08:11.690
Pierre!

08:12.700 --> 08:16.560
Amoro, France's goalkeeper, has now taken his place.

08:17.210 --> 08:21.180
Against him is Hyuga, Japan's ace striker.

08:23.150 --> 08:25.260
Here I go, Tsubasa.

08:25.260 --> 08:26.310
Yes.

08:33.630 --> 08:34.460
Tsubasa!

08:34.990 --> 08:37.880
I used to always think about beating you,

08:37.880 --> 08:40.460
and for that purpose, I used the stormy seas to hone my Tiger Shot.

08:44.520 --> 08:51.060
But now I'd rather wear my number 9 as the world's best ace striker.

09:01.530 --> 09:06.420
This penalty kick will be the first step to realizing my dream as a striker.

09:07.780 --> 09:09.060
Here I go!

09:12.180 --> 09:13.180
It's in!

09:13.180 --> 09:16.570
Hyuga, the first Japanese player to shoot, scores!

09:16.570 --> 09:19.480
The goalkeeper, Amoro, didn't even move.

09:21.220 --> 09:23.770
France and Japan are tied 1-1.

09:23.770 --> 09:26.430
Here's France's Bossi, to take their second penalty.

09:27.540 --> 09:29.500
I'll stop it this time.

09:33.980 --> 09:37.490
Oh! Wakashimazu reacted, but he couldn't stop it!

09:37.490 --> 09:39.440
It's now 2-1.

09:40.100 --> 09:44.100
Wakashimazu does seem to be held back by the injury to his right hand!

09:47.040 --> 09:48.720
The next one's mine.

09:50.850 --> 09:52.580
Matsuyama-kun!

09:52.580 --> 09:56.410
The second Japanese shooter will be Matsuyama, who is from the Hokkaido region.

09:56.410 --> 09:59.580
He's wearing a headband to prove his determination.

09:59.580 --> 10:01.220
Fujisawa,

10:01.220 --> 10:07.300
I wonder if you're watching me on this pitch from somewhere in France.

10:12.500 --> 10:15.540
Hey, Fujisawa! Your hands are really red! Are you okay?

10:20.530 --> 10:22.320
S-Sorry!

10:22.320 --> 10:23.380
Don't be!

10:24.590 --> 10:26.700
After the semifinal of the national tournament,

10:27.670 --> 10:29.460
if I had won,

10:29.460 --> 10:33.200
I was going to declare my feelings for you before you left for France.

10:34.180 --> 10:37.710
But I wasn't able to win.

10:40.620 --> 10:44.260
I'm in France now, Fujisawa!

10:44.260 --> 10:47.900
This time, you'll be able to see me as the winner!

10:48.590 --> 10:50.380
For that...

10:52.520 --> 10:54.620
Nice shot from Matsuyama. This makes it 2-2!

11:13.750 --> 11:16.560
Ferreri scores France's third penalty!

11:16.560 --> 11:20.070
Wakashimazu can't reach it! It's 3-2!

11:20.070 --> 11:26.100
Damn! I didn't want to look pathetic like this in front of you, Wakabayashi.

11:28.820 --> 11:32.930
Misaki Taro, number 11, will be Japan's third to shoot.

11:32.930 --> 11:35.330
It's been three years since I went to France.

11:35.330 --> 11:40.340
I didn't join any club teams because I wanted to be free to return to Japan when I wanted.

11:44.940 --> 11:46.430
Misaki Taro-kun,

11:47.140 --> 11:51.940
Two weeks from now, the Junior Youth Soccer Championship will be held here in France.

11:51.940 --> 11:57.060
I would like you to take part wearing that Number 11 uniform.

11:58.060 --> 12:00.600
Me take part in the Junior Youth Championship?!

12:00.600 --> 12:02.570
I see.

12:02.570 --> 12:04.360
Then it's perfect timing.

12:04.360 --> 12:08.060
We'll settle who has the better technique at the tournament.

12:09.010 --> 12:11.560
Because I hadn't joined any club teams,

12:11.560 --> 12:18.940
I thought that being a part of the Japanese team and playing against Pierre would be impossible.

12:19.530 --> 12:24.580
But I found the answer in this tournament.

12:24.580 --> 12:29.380
Even though I have been indecisive for so long,

12:29.760 --> 12:31.610
I have made my decision!

12:31.610 --> 12:34.380
From here on out, I'll be playing with the Japanese team!

12:36.060 --> 12:38.310
Together with Tsubasa-kun and the others!

12:43.540 --> 12:47.460
Misaki displays splendid control and scores! It's now 3-3!

12:47.460 --> 12:49.860
Nice shot, Misaki-kun!

12:51.820 --> 12:55.620
The fourth penalty taker, Jean Rousto, is taking his place.

12:58.060 --> 13:00.730
Are you gonna shoot to the right, too?

13:00.730 --> 13:04.740
Damn it! They're all aiming to the right because of my injured hand!

13:04.740 --> 13:08.180
Even if I can't catch, I'll be sure to clear!

13:12.540 --> 13:15.150
This time, it's to the opposite side!

13:16.340 --> 13:19.400
We've won the psychological duel!

13:19.400 --> 13:25.390
We've already won, Pierre, since I'm the last to shoot.

13:28.360 --> 13:30.060
Stay strong, Wakashimazu.

13:30.060 --> 13:36.810
If you want to become a world class goalkeeper, you need to have the strength to overcome this obstacle.

13:41.180 --> 13:44.580
Despite being a coach and having a heart condition,

13:44.600 --> 13:49.860
the player to take Japan's fourth penalty is - Misugi!

13:49.860 --> 13:56.460
When I was asked to be in this tournament as a coach, I got a shock I won't forget.

13:58.900 --> 14:00.380
Misugi-kun!

14:00.840 --> 14:01.830
Misugi!

14:01.830 --> 14:04.140
I was so surprised earlier!

14:04.140 --> 14:11.740
If I wasn't chosen because of my heart problems, it means I'm not strong enough,

14:12.500 --> 14:17.370
but it doesn't mean I'm giving up on being part of the Japanese National Team.

14:17.370 --> 14:17.980
Eh?

14:19.040 --> 14:20.980
I have a dream.

14:20.980 --> 14:25.420
A dream where I'm chosen to be on the national team and participate in the International Cup.

14:26.770 --> 14:32.700
Now, not only am I trying to win this match, I am going to gain the strength to fight for my dream!

14:39.410 --> 14:42.410
Nice shot! Such splendid kicking!

14:48.820 --> 14:53.830
Wakabayashi, you've always been in my way.

14:54.510 --> 14:58.700
I've been fighting you as my rival.

14:58.700 --> 15:04.930
But now, it's the French striker in front of me and my own confidence that I need to challenge.

15:06.560 --> 15:10.040
France's fifth to shoot is Napoléon. Will he score with this shot?

15:11.440 --> 15:15.350
If I score, I'll be a hero in France.

15:15.350 --> 15:17.580
I have to score!

15:17.580 --> 15:18.780
Take this!

15:19.620 --> 15:23.980
Even if my right hand ends up getting destroyed, I'll stop this!

15:25.780 --> 15:27.500
Karate Fist Defense!

15:31.540 --> 15:33.180
W-What?!

15:37.580 --> 15:39.560
T-This can't be happening!

15:39.560 --> 15:41.100
How did he...

15:41.100 --> 15:44.320
He stopped it! Wakashimazu finally stopped a shot!

15:44.320 --> 15:46.100
This truly is the karate keeper we know!

15:46.590 --> 15:48.610
You did it, Wakashimazu!

15:48.610 --> 15:53.100
With this, you're a true goalkeeper, and my rival!

15:57.540 --> 15:59.620
We're counting on you, Tsubasa!

15:59.620 --> 16:02.580
It's the last one. Go settle it, Captain!

16:03.250 --> 16:04.390
All right.

16:05.310 --> 16:10.660
And here's Japan's fifth shooter, the captain, Ohzora Tsubasa.

16:10.660 --> 16:15.120
If Ohzora scores, Japan will beat the home team, France, and reach the final.

16:15.120 --> 16:22.830
But if Ohzora misses, we'll continue the shootout until the tie is broken.

16:22.830 --> 16:27.420
Will Ohzora's shot be the one to decide this long game?

16:28.270 --> 16:32.170
Tsubasa. My right hand's completely useless.

16:32.170 --> 16:35.690
You have no other choice but to score!

16:35.690 --> 16:37.420
Wakashimazu!

16:37.420 --> 16:39.420
Nice save!

16:39.420 --> 16:41.980
I'm leaving it up to you, Tsubasa!

16:41.980 --> 16:44.960
Yeah. I'll be sure to score.

16:50.820 --> 16:58.130
Wakashimazu, you sacrificed your right hand to block that ball. Your efforts won't be in vain.

16:58.870 --> 17:02.110
For a player, there's nothing worse than being injured.

17:02.110 --> 17:06.300
I know that well through my experience these last few weeks.

17:08.370 --> 17:11.060
This is about the training camp coming up.

17:11.060 --> 17:12.100
Yes?

17:12.100 --> 17:14.940
You don't need to take part.

17:14.940 --> 17:16.090
Eh?

17:16.090 --> 17:18.380
Your first priority is to heal your shoulder.

17:18.810 --> 17:22.860
That's the most important thing you need to do right now, Ohzora.

17:23.760 --> 17:28.260
My shoulder didn't heal in time, so I couldn't show my abilities.

17:28.260 --> 17:31.040
Unable to go to Europe for the practice games,

17:31.040 --> 17:33.580
I was about to give up on this tournament.

17:34.090 --> 17:36.230
But then, the guys...

17:36.700 --> 17:38.460
Eh?

17:38.460 --> 17:39.940
It's yours.

17:42.220 --> 17:46.460
Everybody knows that the only proper number for Tsubasa is number 10.

17:47.730 --> 17:51.110
It's thanks to the guys that I'm here now.

17:52.060 --> 17:55.470
The guys who trusted me with this number 10.

17:55.470 --> 17:57.710
It was then that I decided,

17:59.270 --> 18:03.190
I would win this tournament at all costs!

18:07.500 --> 18:09.500
You can do it, Tsubasa-kun!

18:10.080 --> 18:11.280
Tsubasa...

18:19.460 --> 18:21.480
Go for it, Tsubasa!

18:21.480 --> 18:23.150
Please score, Tsubasa-kun!

18:23.150 --> 18:23.880
Tsubasa-kun!

18:23.880 --> 18:24.300
Tsubasa!

18:32.250 --> 18:33.620
Tsubasa!

18:41.000 --> 18:42.540
It's in!

18:42.540 --> 18:45.030
Japan has qualified for the final.

18:45.030 --> 18:49.510
Ohzora Tsubasa, the captain of the Japanese team, scored the decisive penalty kick,

18:49.510 --> 18:51.690
resulting in his team winning 5-4 against the home team, France,

18:51.690 --> 18:53.850
and going to the final.

18:54.580 --> 18:55.580
Tsubasa!

18:55.580 --> 18:57.350
We won! We really won!

18:57.350 --> 19:00.060
It's thanks to you, Wakashimazu!

19:03.870 --> 19:05.230
Tsubasa!

19:05.230 --> 19:07.170
You did it, Wakashimazu!

19:07.170 --> 19:08.380
Wakabayashi!

19:08.380 --> 19:10.990
It was truly a difficult game.

19:10.990 --> 19:13.380
Japan was down to ten players after Soda was sent off,

19:13.850 --> 19:16.780
but by giving their all during the second half, and the extra time,

19:16.780 --> 19:21.340
and, lastly, through the penalty shootout, they've won an extraordinary victory!

19:21.910 --> 19:27.380
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

19:27.380 --> 19:29.780
Dear, Tsubasa won!

19:29.780 --> 19:31.980
You did it, Tsubasa-kun!

19:38.980 --> 19:43.900
Damn it! Why did that guy have to stop only my shot!

19:43.900 --> 19:45.790
You put too much into it.

19:45.790 --> 19:46.660
What?

19:47.290 --> 19:51.180
If you had shot like you always do, the ball would've curved.

19:52.350 --> 19:54.180
France lost.

19:54.750 --> 19:58.580
